<details class="performance-notes" id="periodic-calculation-notes">
  <summary>Confirmed Part 1 rules and data coverage</summary>
  <p>The Tickets and Returns definitions have been confirmed. Time definitions remain pending. Reports recalculate using current fields and permissions; later edits can change past results.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Includes every day from RSD through RED. Beginning debt uses status at the end of the day before RSD, open with current due date before RSD. New is not an excluded status for this Periodic report.</li>
    <li>Current Ticket Owner governs all attribution, including old periods. Current blank owners stay unassigned. Current due date, tracker, priority and visible Complexity Weight apply; later edits can change historical results.</li>
    <li>Responsibility starts at the latest recorded To-Do on/before RED during the current owner's uninterrupted tenure. Reassignment invalidates evidence from an earlier tenure. Same-journal owner/status changes use the resulting owner. Missing To-Do history is disclosed, never replaced with creation time. Owner-assignment evidence remains separate audit information.</li>
    <li>Category precedence is beginning debt, then hotfix, then planned task. Tickets already closed before RSD are outside expectation. Planned tasks have a current due date within the period, including assignments made before RSD and tickets created during the period.</li>
    <li>Hotfix means current Immediate/Hot Fix priority, latest To-Do for the current owner during the period, and a required current due date on/before RED. Urgent/Current Week alone is not a hotfix. No missing-date fallback is applied. Valid current due dates schedule expectation, bounded at RSD; opening debt is present at the opening point.</li>
    <li>Current Archived, Ongoing and On-Hold remove tickets from the entire package, with linked exclusions. Expected tickets excluded by an in-period status change have a separate explanation list. Beginning debt requires open status at the opening boundary; historical On-Hold/Ongoing does not override current eligibility.</li>
    <li>Delivery requires recorded Done / Closed within RSD–RED, Done / Closed at RED, and still Done / Closed now. Reopening after RED removes delivery from historical reports too. Each ticket counts once using its latest completion by RED. Missing completion evidence remains unresolved expectation debt and is linked for review.</li>
    <li>Extraordinary tickets disclose recorded owner changes, deadline changes, repeated To-Do entries and reopening after Done. Initial owner/due assignments do not count as changes. Available history includes later changes; unrecorded or undefined irregular activities cannot be detected. Scheduled-work drill-downs distinguish latest To-Do during and before the period without removing commitments with missing history.</li>
    <li>Other Done is qualifying delivery outside the expectation package. It increases Total Actual Done, never Completed from Expectation or its deviation. Logged time, comments and progress alone are not completion.</li>
    <li>Debt at RED = Expected Total minus Completed from Expectation under the current-status checks. Still Open Now is its currently non-closed subset. Current excluded statuses are outside both. Other Work hours in Periodic Time use work-date logs whether or not tickets finish; they are separate from Other Done output.</li>
    <li>Debt targets are zero, while actual beginning-debt workload contributes to expectation. Expected-work deviation is Completed from Expectation minus Expected Total. Debt and Other Done use Plan minus Actual. Total Actual Done has a separate output comparison against Expected Total. Positive is good, negative bad, zero neutral; zero-plan percentages are N/A.</li>
    <li>Counts and usable weights use distinct tickets. Team totals are sums; percentages use those totals, not averages of owner percentages. Missing/hidden/nonpositive/nonfinite weights add no points and are reported separately.</li>
    <li>Other Done additionally qualifies as favorable Extra Work per owner with a nonempty fully delivered expectation and no remaining debt. Team Extra and Unplanned remain separate; raw P−A is retained.</li>
    <li>Trends reuse the final package and current-status checks. Expected follows current due dates, with opening debt at the opening point. Actual follows qualifying recorded completions still Done at RED and now. Monday-based weeks have partial edges; periods over 120 days use month ends. Endpoints reconcile to cards.</li>
    <li>Initial navigation does not scan tickets or history. Apply uses visible projects/issues and visible Ticket Owner fields. Details recalculate the same sets under current permissions; edits between requests may change results. No snapshot database, new custom fields or stored counters are created.</li>
  </ul>
</details>
